CVMA Administrative Hold - 75 Day Compliance Alert

**CVMA APPENDIX C COMPLIANCE NOTICE**

Dear Chapter Executive Board,

This is an automated compliance alert regarding a member currently on Administrative Hold approaching the 90-day maximum period per CVMA Appendix C Section 7.

**MEMBER INFORMATION:**
Name: {!Contact.FirstName} {!Contact.LastName}
Administrative Hold Start Date: {!Contact.Administrative_Hold_Start_Date__c}
Administrative Hold End Date (90 days): {!Contact.Administrative_Hold_End_Date__c}
Days Remaining: 15

**REQUIRED ACTION:**

Per Appendix C Section 7, Administrative Hold may not exceed 90 days without approval from the National Sergeant at Arms (NSAA). The CEB must take ONE of the following actions within 15 days:

1. **Complete Investigation**: Conclude CIC investigation and issue Form 400 (Investigation Decision)
2. **Release from Administrative Hold**: Restore member to active status
3. **Request NSAA Extension**: Submit formal extension request to National Sergeant at Arms
4. **Escalate to SIC**: Elevate investigation to State Investigative Committee (Form 401)

**CURRENT INVESTIGATION STATUS:**
Investigation Committee Type: {!Contact.Investigation_Committee_Type__c}
Investigation Status: {!Contact.Investigation_Status__c}
Committee Chair: {!Contact.Committee_Chair__r.Name}
Investigation POC: {!Contact.POC_Assigned__r.Name}

**FORMS STATUS:**
{!Contact.Investigation_Forms_Status__c}

**NATIONAL BYLAWS COMPLIANCE:**
Failure to comply with the 90-day maximum may result in State or Regional oversight intervention per National Bylaws Article VII.03 chain of command authority.

**IMMEDIATE NEXT STEPS:**
1. Committee Chair schedules emergency CIC meeting
2. Review investigation progress and documentation
3. Determine appropriate action (complete, release, extend, or escalate)
4. Update Salesforce investigation status
5. Notify State Representative of action taken

For questions about Appendix C procedures, contact your State Representative or refer to the CVMA Appendix C Discipline Policy (Rev E, October 2023).

Semper Fi,
CVMA Automated Compliance System

